<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9998" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condĭcĭōnālis</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condit-</span></b> ),
		e, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>with a condition attached, conditional, with conditions</i>
			(freq. in the jurists): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">datio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					34, 4, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">creditores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					50, 16, 54</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 10, 1, 7</span></i>
			 et saep.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">criminatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Jud. 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condĭcĭōnālĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>adv., conditionally</i> (opp. pure,
			simpliciter): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conceptā causā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					25, 1, 17</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">ib. 46, 3, 98, § 5
		al.</span></i></div>
